   "title": "How this works",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Scene state\nSeparates immutable design from changing state. Each shot inherits all preceding changes. Review issues before rendering. Select the shot index on State Ledger; connect its state_before, state_changes, start_cast, end_cast, start_checks, end_checks and design outputs to the corresponding Open Cinema Shot inputs (design \u2192 continuity). The studio uses the same planner and state rules.\n\nAI mode: Normal uses Gemma 4 12B at 8-bit; Fast uses E4B. Change the Open Cinema Writer mode widget. Image and video models stay the same. Cast-review findings retain the saved candidate; inspect it before using it downstream."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
